%S A400761 362880,1140480,2882880,604800,33488640,7660800,193818240,9180864,
%T A400761 24288000,2335132800,142067520,292612320,14354081280,1008184320,
%U A400761 527788800,3932712000,99490809600,9190771200,4835376000,25394402880,451562126400,49270636800,25890036480
%N A400761 Product of the 8 nearest neighbors of n in the square spiral.
%C A400761 The neighbors are the four horizontally or vertically adjacent entries and the four diagonally adjacent entries.
%C A400761 16 divides a(n) for every n, since exactly four of the eight neighbors are even.
%C A400761 For n >= 2, n^2 - 1 divides a(n), since n-1 and n+1 are both neighbors of n.
%C A400761 a(n) ~ n^8, since each of the eight neighbors differs from n by O(sqrt(n)).
%F A400761 a(n) = n^8 + O(n^(15/2)).
%e A400761 The eight neighbors of 1 are 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, so a(1) = 9! = 362880.
%e A400761 The eight neighbors of 2 are 1, 3, 4, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, so a(2) = 1140480.
%e A400761 The eight neighbors of 9 are 1, 2, 8, 10, 11, 23, 24, 25, so a(9) = 24288000.
%t A400761 m=23; p=FoldList[Plus,0,Flatten@Table[ConstantArray[I^k,Ceiling[k/2]],{k,2 Ceiling[Sqrt[m]]+4}]]; Table[Times@@Pick[Range@Length@p,Abs[p-p[[n]]],1|Sqrt[2]],{n,m}]
%Y A400761 Cf. A214176.
%K A400761 nonn,easy
%O A400761 1,1
